QUESTIONS=[
 'In each case, find an equation of a circle, when the center and radius are: (a) (0,0), r = 4; (b) (3,2), r = 1; (c) (−4,−3), r = 4; (d) (−a,−b), r = a+b.',
 'In each case, determine the equation of a circle using the given information: (a) C(0,0), tangent to x = −5; (b) C(0,0), tangent to y = 6; (c) C(6,−6), circumference passes through the origin; (d) C(−9,−6), circumference passes through (−20,8); (e) C(−5,4), tangent to the x-axis; (f) C(5,3), tangent to the y-axis.',
 'In each case, find the center C(−g,−f) and radius r = √(g²+f²−c) of: (a) x²+y²−8x−6y+9 = 0; (b) 4x²+4y²+16x−12y−7 = 0; (c) x²+y²+4x−6y+13 = 0; (d) x²+y²−x−8y+18 = 0.',
 'In each case, find an equation of a circle which passes through the three points: (a) (−3,0), (5,4), (6,−3); (b) (7,−1), (5,3), (−4,6); (c) (1,2), (3,−4), (5,−6).',
 'In each case, find an equation of a circle which (a) contains the points (2,6), (6,4) and has its center on 3x+2y−1 = 0; (b) contains the points (4,1), (6,5) and has its center on 4x+y−16 = 0.',
 'Find an equation of a circle which passes through (a) (0,0), (0,3) and 4x−5y = 0 is tangent to it at (0,0); (b) (0,−1), (3,0) and 3x+y = 9 is tangent to it at (3,0).',
 'Find an equation of a circle that is concentric to (a) 2x²+2y²+16x−7y = 0 and is tangent to the y-axis; (b) x²+y²−8x+4 = 0 and is tangent to x+2y+6 = 0; (c) x²+y²+6x−10y+33 = 0 and is touching the x-axis.',
 'Find equation of circle which passes through origin and whose intercepts on the coordinate axes are: (a) 3 and 4; (b) 2 and 4.'
]
STEPS=[
 ['Use (x−h)²+(y−k)² = r² for center (h,k) and radius r.','(a) h = k = 0 and r² = 16, giving x²+y² = 16.','(b) Substitute h = 3, k = 2 and r² = 1: (x−3)²+(y−2)² = 1.','(c) Substitute h = −4, k = −3 and r² = 16: (x+4)²+(y+3)² = 16.','(d) Substitute h = −a, k = −b: (x+a)²+(y+b)² = (a+b)².','The stated radius in (d) requires a+b > 0 for a nondegenerate circle. If a+b = 0 this is a point; if a+b < 0 it cannot be the stated radius, although the squared equation has radius |a+b|.'],
 ['For tangency, the radius equals the perpendicular distance from the center to the line; for a given circumference point it equals the center-to-point distance.','(a) Distance from (0,0) to x = −5 is 5, giving x²+y² = 25.','(b) Distance from (0,0) to y = 6 is 6, giving x²+y² = 36.','(c) The squared distance from (6,−6) to (0,0) is 36+36 = 72, giving (x−6)²+(y+6)² = 72.','(d) The displacement from (−9,−6) to (−20,8) is (−11,14), whose squared length is 121+196 = 317; hence (x+9)²+(y+6)² = 317.','(e) Distance from (−5,4) to the x-axis is 4, giving (x+5)²+(y−4)² = 16.','(f) Distance from (5,3) to the y-axis is 5, giving (x−5)²+(y−3)² = 25. Each tangent line has exactly one circle contact at the perpendicular projection of its center.'],
 ['Normalize the coefficients of x² and y² to 1, then read the center as (−g,−f) and squared radius as g²+f²−c.','(a) g = −4, f = −3, c = 9, so center (4,3) and r² = 16+9−9 = 16: r = 4.','(b) Divide by 4: x²+y²+4x−3y−7/4 = 0.','Thus g = 2, f = −3/2, c = −7/4, giving center (−2,3/2) and r² = 4+9/4+7/4 = 8: r = 2√2.','(c) Center (−2,3) and r² = 4+9−13 = 0. The completed equation is (x+2)²+(y−3)² = 0, a single point.','(d) Center (1/2,4) and r² = 1/4+16−18 = −7/4.','Since a sum of two real squares cannot be negative, (d) has no real circle or real radius. Its formal complex radius is i√7/2; the real locus is empty.'],
 ['Use x²+y²+2gx+2fy+c = 0 and substitute the three points to get three linear equations in g,f,c.','(a) The equations are −6g+c = −9, 10g+8f+c = −41, and 12g−6f+c = −45. Solving gives g = −2, f = 0, c = −21.','Thus x²+y²−4x−21 = 0, equivalent to (x−2)²+y² = 25. The three squared center distances are 25,25,25.','(b) The equations are 14g−2f+c = −50, 10g+6f+c = −34, and −8g+12f+c = −52. Solving gives g = 2, f = 3, c = −72.','Thus x²+y²+4x+6y−72 = 0, equivalent to (x+2)²+(y+3)² = 85. The three squared center distances are 85,85,85.','(c) The equations are 2g+4f+c = −5, 6g−8f+c = −25, and 10g−12f+c = −61. Solving gives g = −11, f = −2, c = 25.','Thus x²+y²−22x−4y+25 = 0, equivalent to (x−11)²+(y−2)² = 100. The three squared center distances are 100,100,100.','Each triple is non-collinear (cross products −60,30,8 respectively), so the linear systems determine unique circles. Direct substitution gives zero in every stated source-point equation.'],
 ['Let C(h,k) be the center. Equate its squared distances to the two given points, then combine with the prescribed center line.','(a) Equidistance from (2,6) and (6,4) simplifies to 2h−k = 3.','Combine with 3h+2k = 1: k = 2h−3, hence 7h−6 = 1 and (h,k) = (1,−1).','The squared radius is (2−1)²+(6+1)² = 50. Thus (x−1)²+(y+1)² = 50. The other point also has squared distance 25+25 = 50.','(b) Equidistance from (4,1) and (6,5) simplifies to h+2k = 11.','Combine with 4h+k = 16 to get (h,k) = (3,4).','The squared radius is (4−3)²+(1−4)² = 10, so (x−3)²+(y−4)² = 10. The other point gives 9+1 = 10.','Both centers satisfy their specified lines, verifying the third condition as well as the two circumference conditions.'],
 ['At a specified tangency point, the radius vector must be parallel to the tangent line’s normal. First check that each claimed contact lies on its line.','(a) The origin lies on 4x−5y = 0. Equal distances from center (h,k) to (0,0) and (0,3) give k = 3/2.','Parallelism of (h,k) to normal (4,−5) gives 5h+4k = 0, hence h = −6/5.','The squared radius is 36/25+9/4 = 369/100. Expanding the standard form gives x²+y²+(12/5)x−3y = 0.','Both source points satisfy that equation, and the radius dot tangent direction (5,4) is 5(−6/5)+4(3/2) = 0.','(b) The contact (3,0) lies on 3x+y = 9. Equal distances to (0,−1) and (3,0) give 3h+k = 4.','Parallelism of (h−3,k) to the normal (3,1) gives h−3 = 3k. Solving yields (h,k) = (3/2,−1/2).','Its squared radius is 5/2, giving x²+y²−3x+y = 0. Both source points satisfy it, and the radius dot tangent direction (1,−3) is −3/2+3/2 = 0.'],
 ['Concentric circles share a center, but the new radius must be calculated from the specified tangent condition.','(a) Divide by 2 to obtain x²+y²+8x−(7/2)y = 0, whose center is (−4,7/4).','Distance to the y-axis is 4, so (x+4)²+(y−7/4)² = 16.','(b) Completing squares in x²+y²−8x+4 = 0 gives center (4,0).','Its distance to x+2y+6 = 0 is |4+0+6|/√5 = 2√5, hence (x−4)²+y² = 20.','(c) Completing squares gives center (−3,5). Distance to the x-axis is 5, so (x+3)²+(y−5)² = 25.','In every case the new circle’s radius equals the center-to-line distance, establishing tangency while retaining the original center.'],
 ['A circle through the origin has general form x²+y²+Dx+Ey = 0 because its constant term is zero.','Taking the listed values as the signed x and y intercepts, use the other two points (a,0) and (0,b).','Substitution gives a²+Da = 0 and b²+Eb = 0. Since these intercepts are nonzero, D = −a and E = −b.','(a) With intercepts 3 and 4, the equation is x²+y²−3x−4y = 0. Its center is (3/2,2) and radius is 5/2.','(b) With intercepts 2 and 4, the equation is x²+y²−2x−4y = 0. Its center is (1,2) and radius is √5.','The origin and both axis-intercept points satisfy their equations. If the source instead intended unsigned intercept lengths, independent sign choices would give additional reflected circles; the positive signed convention is stated here.']
]
ANSWERS=['(a) x²+y² = 16; (b) (x−3)²+(y−2)² = 1; (c) (x+4)²+(y+3)² = 16; (d) (x+a)²+(y+b)² = (a+b)², with a+b > 0.','(a) x²+y² = 25; (b) x²+y² = 36; (c) (x−6)²+(y+6)² = 72; (d) (x+9)²+(y+6)² = 317; (e) (x+5)²+(y−4)² = 16; (f) (x−5)²+(y−3)² = 25.','(a) C(4,3), r = 4; (b) C(−2,3/2), r = 2√2; (c) point circle (−2,3), r = 0; (d) no real points, formal center (1/2,4).','(a) x²+y²−4x−21 = 0; (b) x²+y²+4x+6y−72 = 0; (c) x²+y²−22x−4y+25 = 0.','(a) (x−1)²+(y+1)² = 50; (b) (x−3)²+(y−4)² = 10.','(a) x²+y²+(12/5)x−3y = 0; (b) x²+y²−3x+y = 0.','(a) (x+4)²+(y−7/4)² = 16; (b) (x−4)²+y² = 20; (c) (x+3)²+(y−5)² = 25.','(a) x²+y²−3x−4y = 0; (b) x²+y²−2x−4y = 0, using positive signed intercepts.']
